WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:15.367
Unit sixteen: Writing Emails. In this unit, you will write a polite email with the right parts.

4
00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.233
Email.

5
00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:20.490
Email means a message you send on the internet.

6
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.732
I wrote an email to my teacher.

7
00:00:23.432 --> 00:00:26.502
Your turn. Say: Email.

8
00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:29.994
Email.

9
00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:31.915
Subject.

10
00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:34.777
Subject means the title of an email.

11
00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:36.984
The subject is 'Homework question'.

12
00:00:37.684 --> 00:00:40.371
Your turn. Say: Subject.

13
00:00:43.071 --> 00:00:43.967
Subject.

14
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:45.799
Dear.

15
00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:48.754
Dear means a word to begin a letter or email.

16
00:00:49.054 --> 00:00:50.368
Dear Mr. Jake, ...

17
00:00:51.068 --> 00:00:53.094
Your turn. Say: Dear.

18
00:00:55.794 --> 00:00:56.423
Dear.

19
00:00:57.417 --> 00:00:58.302
Paragraph.

20
00:00:59.002 --> 00:01:02.151
Paragraph means a group of sentences about one idea.

21
00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:04.462
My email has two paragraphs.

22
00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:07.443
Your turn. Say: Paragraph.

23
00:01:10.143 --> 00:01:11.120
Paragraph.

24
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:13.106
Attach.

25
00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:16.084
Attach means to add a file to an email.

26
00:01:16.384 --> 00:01:17.757
I attached my homework.

27
00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:20.784
Your turn. Say: Attach.

28
00:01:23.484 --> 00:01:24.439
Attach.

29
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:26.416
Reply.

30
00:01:27.116 --> 00:01:30.161
Reply means to answer an email or message.

31
00:01:30.461 --> 00:01:31.857
Please reply soon.

32
00:01:32.557 --> 00:01:35.371
Your turn. Say: Reply.

33
00:01:38.071 --> 00:01:38.887
Reply.

34
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:40.966
Best wishes.

35
00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:44.443
Best wishes means a friendly way to end an email.

36
00:01:44.743 --> 00:01:46.290
Best wishes, Sreypich

37
00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.141
Your turn. Say: Best wishes.

38
00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:53.982
Best wishes.

39
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:55.799
Send.

40
00:01:56.499 --> 00:01:58.823
Send means to make a message go to someone.

41
00:01:59.123 --> 00:02:00.763
Click here to send the email.

42
00:02:01.463 --> 00:02:03.721
Your turn. Say: Send.

43
00:02:06.421 --> 00:02:07.166
Send.

44
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.115
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:10.415 --> 00:02:13.262
Sreypich, how do you start an email to a teacher?

46
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.294
I start with 'Dear Mr. Jake'.

47
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:19.130
What do you write next?

48
00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.370
I'm writing to ask about the homework.

49
00:02:23.683 --> 00:02:25.160
And how do you finish it?

50
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.857
I write 'Best wishes' and my name. Then I click send.

51
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.428
Grammar focus: I'm writing to.

52
00:02:33.728 --> 00:02:35.623
I'm writing to ask about the homework.

53
00:02:35.923 --> 00:02:39.397
Use 'I'm writing to...' in the first sentence to give the reason for your email.

54
00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:43.291
Now read and listen. An Email to My Teacher.

55
00:02:43.591 --> 00:02:44.708
Dear Mr. Jake,

56
00:02:46.017 --> 00:02:48.399
I'm writing to ask about our English project.

57
00:02:49.683 --> 00:02:52.426
I have attached my first paragraph to this email.

58
00:02:53.717 --> 00:02:56.204
Could you please reply and tell me if it is correct?

59
00:02:57.517 --> 00:02:59.040
Best wishes, Sreypich.

60
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.014
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:03.314 --> 00:03:05.163
I'm writing blank ask a question.

62
00:03:05.463 --> 00:03:08.396
A, to. B, for. C, at.

63
00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:14.487
The answer is A: to.

64
00:03:15.983 --> 00:03:18.575
The title of an email is the blank.

65
00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:22.528
A, subject. B, paragraph. C, reply.

66
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:28.296
The answer is A: subject.

67
00:03:29.783 --> 00:03:31.922
To add a file to an email is to blank.

68
00:03:32.222 --> 00:03:35.980
A, attach. B, send. C, reply.

69
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:42.505
The answer is A: attach.

70
00:03:44.017 --> 00:03:48.042
Now it's your turn to speak. Who do you write emails to? Why?

71
00:03:53.342 --> 00:04:00.664
I write emails to my teacher. For example, I'm writing to ask about homework. I always start with 'Dear' and end with 'Best wishes'.

72
00:04:00.964 --> 00:04:02.661
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.952
Great work today! You learned eight new words and i'm writing to.

74
00:04:07.252 --> 00:04:11.437
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

75
00:04:11.737 --> 00:04:14.320
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.156
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

